module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Tits.MinimumIndex.LargeTwoOvergroups.SeedOvergroups.Geometry.CommonFactorCover.FactorData
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Tits.MinimumIndex.LargeTwoOvergroups.SeedOvergroups.Geometry.Reduction

/-!
# Every common factor belongs to every listed place

The source generators are tested for membership using the certified inverse
maps. Every remaining factor is a generator times an earlier factor, as
certified at the three-point base. Strong induction proves membership of
all literal factors, without any seed-order assumption.

The same descent puts the factors in the subgroup generated by those source
generators. Equality with that subgroup is a separate coverage obligation.
Source: Parrott (1972), §5, p.683 and the original seed witnesses.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Tits.MinimumIndex.LargeTwoOvergroups.SeedOvergroups.Geometry.CommonFactorCover
set_option Elab.async false

private theorem shape_checked (t : Fin 18) :
    (factorSteps t).map Prod.fst = factorIndices t := by
  revert t
  apply Atlas1600OrderCertificate.allFin
  decide +kernel

